-- title:
--   Theorem 1, p. 5 — a joint mix whose blocks are conditionally independent given S_A, with increasing conditional expectations, is NA
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathbf X=(X_1,\dots,X_n)$ be a joint mix, i.e. $\sum_{i=1}^nX_i$ is almost surely constant, and write $S_A=\sum_{i\in A}X_i$ for $A\subseteq[n]$. Suppose that for every $A\subseteq[n]$:
--
--   1. (a) $\mathbf X_A$ and $\mathbf X_{[n]\setminus A}$ are independent conditionally on $S_A$;
--   2. (b) $\mathbb E[f(\mathbf X_A)\mid S_A]$ is increasing in $S_A$ for every coordinatewise increasing $f:\mathbb R^A\to\mathbb R$ with $f(\mathbf X_A)$ integrable: there is $g:\mathbb R\to\mathbb R$, increasing on a set $T$ with $\mathbb P(S_A\in T)=1$, such that $\mathbb E[f(\mathbf X_A)\mid S_A]=g(S_A)$ almost surely.
--
--   Then $\mathbf X$ is negatively associated:
--
--   $$\operatorname{Cov}\big(f(\mathbf X_A),g(\mathbf X_B)\big)\le0$$
--
--   for all disjoint $A,B\subseteq[n]$ and all coordinatewise increasing $f,g$ with $f(\mathbf X_A),g(\mathbf X_B)$ square integrable.
--
--   The theorem gives a sufficient condition for a joint mix to be NA. It replaces the independence assumption of Joag-Dev and Proschan (1983, Theorem 2.6) by conditional independence.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $\mathbf X$ is represented by its law $P$ on $\mathbb R^n$ with 0-based coordinates. Conditional independence is Mathlib's `CondIndepFun` given the σ-algebra generated by $S_A$, applied to the coordinate maps $x\mapsto x_A$ and $x\mapsto x_{A^c}$. Hypotheses (a) and (b) are required for every $A$, including $\emptyset$ and $[n]$.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: a random vector X = (X_1, …, X_n) with components indexed by [n] → its law P on Fin n → ℝ, coordinates 0-based; reason: every notion involved depends on X only through its law; same instances
--   - reading: E[f(X_A)|S_A] is increasing in S_A for every increasing function f → for every coordinatewise increasing f with f(X_A) integrable, the conditional expectation given σ(S_A) equals g(S_A) a.s. for some g increasing on a set carrying S_A almost surely; reason: the conditional expectation exists only for integrable f(X_A) and is defined up to null sets; an increasing version is required only on the support of S_A
--   - reading: f(X_A), g(X_B) have finite second moments (Definition 1(iv)) → MemLp 2 of f(X_A) and g(X_B), with no separate measurability condition on f, g; reason: finite second moment presupposes that f(X_A) is a random variable; MemLp contains exactly almost-everywhere measurability
--   - generalization: vectors of positive dimension n → n : ℕ, including n = 0; reason: at n = 0 both blocks are empty and all tests are constants, so NA holds; all positive-dimensional source instances are retained
-- source:
--   Koike, Lin & Wang, Joint mixability and notions of negative dependence, arXiv:2204.11438v4, p. 5, Theorem 1 (proof p. 22)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_JointMixND_QuadOT_Basic
import Definitions.Def_JointMixND_QuadOT_Supplement_Dependence

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory

namespace JointMixND.QuadOT.Supplement

theorem theorem_1 {n : ℕ} (P : Measure (Fin n → ℝ)) [IsProbabilityMeasure P]
    (hJM : IsJointMix P)
    (ha : ∀ A : Finset (Fin n),
      CondIndepFun (MeasurableSpace.comap (sumOver A) inferInstance)
        (measurable_sumOver A).comap_le (restrictTo A) (restrictTo Aᶜ) P)
    (hb : ∀ (A : Finset (Fin n)) (f : (A → ℝ) → ℝ), Monotone f →
      Integrable (fun x => f (restrictTo A x)) P →
      ∃ (g : ℝ → ℝ) (T : Set ℝ), (∀ᵐ x ∂P, sumOver A x ∈ T) ∧ MonotoneOn g T ∧
        P[fun x => f (restrictTo A x) | MeasurableSpace.comap (sumOver A) inferInstance]
          =ᵐ[P] fun x => g (sumOver A x)) :
    IsNA P := by sorry

end JointMixND.QuadOT.Supplement
